Package: BSS
Type: Package
Title: BSS
Version: 0.5.0
Date: 2026-10-11
Author: Rafael Lambertucci
Maintainer: Rafael Lambertucci <rlambertucci@unifesp.br>
Description: This module provides a comprehensive suite of advanced statistical procedures for behavioral and health sciences: 
  1) Network analysis for continuous and mixed data with bridge centrality and community detection; 
  2) Missing value patterns and data imputation using missRanger and MICE with Rubin rules pooling;
  3) Outlier detection using Dixon's Q, Hubert adjusted boxplot, modified z-score, and multivariate Mahalanobis/MCD;
  4) Descriptive discriminant analysis (DDA) with Box's M test and classification matrix LOOCV; 
  5) Aligned Rank Transform (ART) nonparametric factorial ANOVA with Partial Omega-Squared, FDR multiplicity control, and interaction plots;
  6) Pairwise effect sizes, Sawilowsky benchmark, multi-metric conversions, and forest plots; 
  7) Sample size calculation for finite populations, resource equation, t-test power curves, TOST equivalence, and proportions; 
  8) Correlation comparison for independent and dependent coefficients with Jennrich matrix test and CI plots;
  9) Power and bounded transformations for normality (Box-Cox, Yeo-Johnson, Johnson curves, Arcsine, and Logit) with Anderson-Darling and Shapiro-Francia tests;
  10) Publication-ready group comparison plots, APA 7th HTML export, correlation matrices with significance stars, and clustered heatmaps.
